# INV-11 — invented. Five overs a side: the no-ball kinds the pad offers, and a bowler suspended mid-over.
# Edge cases: a waist-high no-ball and a beamer earn NO free hit (so a bowled
# on the next ball stands: B1 in over 1 after a beamer, B4 after a waist-high
# one), while a front-foot no-ball does (the bowled on it is saved, in both
# innings); a beamer with two off the bat, the umpires suspending the bowler
# for beamers, and another bowler finishing the over (the suspended man's
# no-ball is his, the five balls are the finisher's: 0.1 and 0.5); a run out
# of the non-striker off a waist-high no-ball after a run, at the bowler's
# end (falls at 4.1, the striker stays on strike, no ball of the over); a
# stumping with no keeper on record; the chase won on a no-ball.
# (The pad offers three no-ball kinds: front foot, waist high, beamer. It has
# no "back foot" kind, so that is not scored here.)
match INV-11
title Five overs, the no-ball kinds and a suspension
date 2026-11-11
overs 5
sides Home Away

innings 1 Home
open B1 B2
over BW1  1 nbh+2 . nbbm+1 W:b 4 . 1
over BW2  2 nb W:b 1 wd+1 W:c/F3 4 1
over BW3  3 nbbm+2 susp:beamers bw:BW4/suspended . 4 6 1 W:lbw
over BW1  1 wd . nb W:b 2 1 W:c/F6
over BW2  4 nbh+1&W:ro/F4,ns,end=b . 2 nbh W:b 1 W:st/F1

innings 2 Away
open B1 B2
over BW1  6 nbbm W:c/F9 nb 6 4 1 .
over BW2  . wd 2 W:lbw nbh+2 W:b 4 2
over BW3  1 W:c/F3 4 wd+1 3 1b nb+4 W:b
over BW1  1 2 . W:c/F2 1 2
over BW2  . W:b 1 W:c/F5 nb+1

